Stark Rust backend

Behavioral compatibility and test fixtures for `apply_patch`, the `execpolicy`
prefix-rule/decision engine, and unified-exec head/tail output buffering are
derived from OpenAI Codex (https://github.com/openai/codex), licensed under
Apache-2.0.

`backend-rs/vendor/portable-pty` is portable-pty 0.9.0
(https://github.com/wez/wezterm/tree/main/pty), Copyright (c) 2018 Wez Furlong,
licensed under MIT. It is vendored with two local fixes: ConPTY is created with
the resize-quirk flag only (avoiding cursor/inherit-input hangs), and
TerminateProcess result handling is corrected.

Code Mode follows OpenCode v2 (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode,
`packages/codemode` 2.4.1, dev commit 9964772), licensed under MIT.
`backend-rs/codemode-worker` runs `@opencode/codemode` 2.4.1 and
`psychoscript` 0.2.1 (both MIT) on Bun; `crates/stark-tools/src/codemode`
ports OpenCode's catalog summary, `# Code Mode` instructions, background-job
notice and restart recovery, incremental catalog instructions, result
formatting and `ToolOutput` truncation/spill, progress publications, diff
budgets, fetch/path/Bun extensions,
OpenAI freeform/custom-tool wire encoding (including the fixed
`tool/patch-grammar.txt` Lark grammar and the `<system-update>` lowering), and
the JSON-Schema-to-TypeScript signature renderer. Differential fixtures in
`backend-rs/codemode-worker/test/opencode-parity` run the real 2.4.1 source
under Bun to generate the Rust tests' expected bytes. The runtime's
tool admission, idempotent calls, and snapshot suspend/resume are unchanged in
the library; the application, like OpenCode, does not persist Code Mode
programs across a server restart.
